OpenWings patch 0020: OpenWings looks (type, shapes and textures, not only colors)

Upstream's themes recolor one layout; two of them are named after other
products. OpenWings themes, named ow-*, also restyle type, shapes, borders
and textures through one stylesheet (wings/brand/skins.css, served as
/static/openwings/skins.css), which applies only under
html[data-ow-skin="<theme name>"], so upstream's themes look exactly as
before.

  * static/index.html: the early boot script loads the stylesheet and
    marks the saved look (or the default) before the first paint.
  * static/js/theme.js: the OpenWings themes, and applyOpenWingsSkin(),
    which save() calls whenever a theme is chosen.

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later (same as upstream)

